  "mathematical_claims": [
    "For the odd-core channelization, every live channel amplitude has absolute value at most one.",
    "The whole-channel weighted energy satisfies 0 <= E_N^odd <= H_N/2.",
    "Hence E_N^odd <= ((1+1/eta)/2)*(N+1)^eta for every eta>0.",
    "The occupied-channel count is ceil(N/2), so generic channel Cauchy returns only a rate-one allowance.",
    "The full discrete supplier is equivalent to all-positive-rate upper control of the complete signed cross-channel packet once the channel-energy bound is supplied."
  ],
